[{:db/id "q-9980/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "42c0d506-1aa1-50f1-925f-3776c434998d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "88d0c1ad-2e69-53e8-b0f1-14231d6b6c48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "104c5573-009e-55dc-872f-3406140f4ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b92df9bf-57f8-52c4-bdb1-778f42842a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "30d4d4f3-edf3-50e0-b558-676c2c519051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "32185872-743f-5625-abaf-14cc3904b386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9980/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-9980/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-9980/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-9980/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-9980/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-9980/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9980" :question/id #uuid "b53bfca7-a35b-5bdd-8a26-779771b1f95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9980" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9980/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "4e80adb5-d2d0-5375-ac8e-96c908f4c86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" :answer/id #uuid "b5b15967-d3ef-551a-947f-bfb28904e4a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "debcc437-3577-57c9-b607-c2c9c289e770" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "28e902a6-5051-5cca-b30e-0fee2f148317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "a47b88ad-e6a3-548e-b3a7-95ede04a074e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3906e258-840c-5de5-af0e-44d141899def" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18284/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer-field/choices ["q-18284/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-18284/selection/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" "q-18284/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-18284/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-18284/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18284" :question/id #uuid "760ba6ba-f519-5e68-b2c7-ade22689c6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18284" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $-16.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22}=\\frac{1}{-16}\\cdot 4=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18284/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "7cd800ed-e50c-554d-9737-eeda0629a09b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "69b0dac9-0505-5959-b6b1-5693c223ec42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4ed7a78d-bd89-5f9b-94b1-6f24d665fcd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "88892a86-3a54-5a28-8119-ff95f09f7e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0cfddfff-2efc-5935-a57b-be628caa2616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b32d26-4ce1-5e64-80c3-4102cfcaad63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73542/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73542/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-73542/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-73542/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-73542/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-73542/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73542" :question/id #uuid "f2b1695b-282d-54b6-9ac9-0c3ba20a588b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73542" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275755/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "43a3fbd2-7f9b-5efe-b807-f44b9545e81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275755/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ee3e2b62-ecd3-52a1-9ef1-f87f4614c55c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275755/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "197b5c36-1e0b-5239-8e5a-8e1d24c83ee2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275755/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-275755/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-275755/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275755" :question/id #uuid "7fedf1ce-1d8a-575c-bbd4-9093e6ecd764" :question/math-academy-id "q-275755" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2+2)-0-3(2-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(6-0) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275755/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275755"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319413/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd" :answer/id #uuid "55b1616d-08df-5ad7-ba02-103428efcd35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319413/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb06bcc-74a6-5677-a4f1-bd2028bab163" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319413/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd" :answer-field/choices ["q-319413/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319413" :question/id #uuid "bfe6bc14-6591-5f71-bb33-e7e4cf7f033e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319413/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
